  "body": "## What changed\n\nA new depth operation (2D Contour, Pocket, Adaptive, Offset…, quick-added from the ribbon) took its default **bottom** from `Carried::of`'s fallback, `WorkOffset(0) + 0`: the G54 Z0 plane. With G54 Z zeroed on the **part's top**, which is a common shop habit (Tormach users in #131 do it) and what *Set origin* on a top face produces, that bottom resolved level with the default top (`TopOfModel + 0`). `CreateOperation` then refused the zero-depth operation (\"must cut downward…\") before the user could open its Heights tab, so the only way through was to move G54 temporarily.\n\nThe fallback is now **`BottomOfModel + 0`** (`crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs`, one line). A fresh operation's numbers still show where the material is, which was the intent of the old default (\"issue 2\"'s contract in the test comment), but without depending on the shop's work-offset convention.\n\n**This reverses a deliberate default.** `fresh_depth_operations_default_to_the_part_and_g54` pinned the G54 bottom. It is renamed to `fresh_depth_operations_default_to_the_part_top_and_bottom` and updated, with the reason in its comment.\n\n**Edge case, unchanged by this PR:** a model with zero thickness (top = bottom) still seeds a zero-depth operation. It did before too, whenever G54 sat on that plane.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` ran in batch mode, because the comparison base was older than upstream. **Clippy with `-D warnings`: clean.** geometry, cl, tools, post and sim: all ok. Failures that also occur on this branch's upstream base without the change:\n  - `motion::swarf_pose_continuity`: `advanced_swarf_poses_never_flip_between_consecutive_cuts` and `no_swarf_pose_under_the_equator_is_upright_and_every_flank_clears_the_blade`. Checked on the base commit e607ca1; no open issue tracks them.\n  - `app::drilling_cross_box` / `drilling_cross_spindle`: #151.\n  - `ui`: the three headless-GPU tests (`headless_run_succeeds`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`). There's no fallback graphics adapter on this macOS machine.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib`: 239 passed (the headless one aside), including the new and updated tests. App suites that seed through `Carried`/`retype_params` (`mill2d_b`, `area_open`, `whole_model_pocket`, `shoulder_adaptive`, `roughing2d`, `pick_doors`, `heights`): all pass.\n- Merges cleanly with current `upstream/main`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::fresh_op_tests::a_fresh_depth_operation_is_created_with_g54_on_the_part_top`: the ribbon's own `quick_params` for kinds 1–4, created through `CreateOperation` on a part with G54 placed on its top. This fails with the old default.\n- `egui_app::fresh_op_tests::a_bottom_on_the_g54_plane_is_refused_when_g54_sits_on_the_part_top`: the old default reproduced explicitly, still refused (\"must cut downward\"), documenting the failure #214 reported.\n- `operations::height_row_tests::fresh_depth_operations_default_to_the_part_top_and_bottom`: updated (it was `…_part_and_g54`).\n\nChangelog: A new depth operation's default bottom is the part's floor (Bottom of model), not the G54 plane, so it is created even when G54 Z is zeroed on the part top\n\nFixes #214\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
